; Bill pay: each bank debit from the bill-pay service pays several bills at
; once. The debits come from the checking feed and the bills from the
; service's own export; both land on transfers:billpay. Kept in its own file,
; included last, so the other feeds' transaction numbers do not move.

; One $2,247.50 debit paying a $2,000.00 and a $247.50 bill the same day:
; the only two bills that sum to it, so Find Matches suggests the three as
; one combination (plan 35 Amendment A4).

2027-01-12 * BILL.COM PAYABLES
    assets:checking                 $-2,247.50
    transfers:billpay                $2,247.50

2027-01-12 * Northside Builders invoice 1042
    expenses:contractors             $2,000.00
    transfers:billpay               $-2,000.00

2027-01-12 * City Water & Power
    expenses:utilities                 $247.50
    transfers:billpay                 $-247.50

